    <string name="shizuku_note">The advanced engine needs "record screen/audio" authorization (Android 10+ capture API); Bluetooth headphones work too; about 80–120 ms latency. Panning = duplicate a channel and swing L/R gains; binaural = orbit a source using binaural cues. The lightweight engine has zero latency but only L/R panning.</string>
    <string name="channel_name">Surround service</string>
    <string name="settings_title">Settings &amp; keep-alive</string>
    <string name="github_repo">View source on GitHub</string>
    <string name="main_note">Lightweight engine: adjusts system output gains in real time, no capture or replay, zero latency and no doubling; L/R panning — defaults 20 / 20 / 1 work immediately.\nAdvanced engine: captures and re-plays processed audio (original muted, ~80–120 ms latency), with panning (mono + swing) or binaural (spatialized orbiting) options.</string>

